Author: Marcel Rød <marcelroed@gmail.com>
Date:   Mon Jul 20 11:56:24 2026 -0700

    Match HF drop semantics for byte-gap BPE vocabs
    
    HF tokenizers' BPE with unk_token: null silently drops a symbol that has
    no vocab entry when building a word, and the dropped symbol's neighbors
    then merge with each other (Hy3 has no single-byte 0x0D token, so
    "\r\n\r\n" encodes exactly like "\n\n" — one merged token). tencent/Hy3
    (the most-used model on OpenRouter) ships such a vocab, and gigatoken's
    byte remapping refused to load it.
    
    ByteRemapping now takes a MissingBytePolicy: the tokenizer.json loader
    passes Drop when model.unk_token is null, keeping the load error for
    tiktoken-style vocabs and for the (never observed) gapped-with-unk
    combination. Dropped bytes are compacted out of the symbol sequence
    before the merge loop. Vocabs whose only gaps are the never-in-UTF-8
    bytes keep the existing placeholder fill, and complete vocabs keep the
    straight-line remap loops: the compacting variant is gated on a per-call
    has_drops branch, and the four hand-rolled remap loops collapse into
    shared remap_short_any/remap_extend_any helpers.
    
    Validated exact vs HF on tencent/Hy3 and tencent/Hy3-preview (full
    battery + 2 MB OWT), with DeepSeek-V4/GLM-5.2/gpt-oss/Qwen3.6 staying
    exact as remapping-sensitive sanity checks.
    
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HrFddQSsxumgFV2nHHxrwS

